    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI implemented `initials` as a computed, read-only field on the Owner response:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` plus a default helper:\n   ```java\n   default String initials(Owner owner) {\n       return Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n               + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nSo an owner named \"john smith\" now serializes with `\"initials\": \"J.S.\"`, matching the spec (upper-cased first letters, dot-separated, trailing dot). The existing `RespondWithOwner` function and pipeline already route through the mapper, so no wiring changes were needed.",
